fix(reconciler): make the keyed allocation win pool-member materialization

The allocation-ownership seam (ga-f7v2ft.126's cutover arm), built with the
ga-ij8mh round-6 stand-down template at its own effect boundary.

Before this, the two pool builders were only mutually exclusive AFTER a member
existed: revalidatePlannedPoolMemberDemand re-reads the durable claim the keyed
allocation stamps at CREATE, so first-creator-wins - and legacy, planning from
a per-tick snapshot and creating immediately, was usually the creator. That is
the 0/0 keyed materialization both arms of the :469 proof recorded, and it is
why the keyed side's ownership was never a yield.

The reservation moves ownership to the moment the exact
(workID, poolTarget, sourceStore) key enters the keyed lane
(enqueueRoutedWorkPoolAllocation), and closes it on every path out of
handleRoutedWorkPoolAllocation - materialized, refused, or failed. The legacy
builder consults the installed seam on CURRENT state at its member-creation
boundary, ahead of the durable claim read, with full-supersede semantics: no
member, no demand.

The one real lapse hazard the round-6 ruling names is bounded structurally
rather than by hope: a reservation carries its reservedAt and retires itself
past routedWorkAllocationReservationLapse, so a controller that stops between
enqueue and handling costs one patrol instead of fencing legacy forever.
Replayed hints coalesce by count so a replay's release cannot retire the
original owner's fence early.

REDs (cmd/gc/pool_allocation_ownership_test.go), the behavioural one proven
non-vacuous by reverting only the consult hunk - legacy materialized worker
gc-1 for the reserved work item:

  - StandsDownForKeyedAllocationReservation: reservation held, no durable claim
    (the exact window first-creator-wins gave legacy) => supersede, zero members
  - ProceedsAfterKeyedAllocationReleases: the no-lapse RED - released
    reservation => legacy materializes on its very next pass
  - ReservationLapsesRatherThanFencingForever: a reservation past the bound is
    retired on read
  - ReservationIsExactKeyed: a different work id, pool target, or source store
    is untouched
  - ReservationCoalescesReplays / LaneReservesAndReleasesAroundTheHandler: the
    seam is driven by the real lane, not by the tests

